# research_feed.py reads this file from your knowledge folder as:
#   <knowledge-dir>/research_sources.txt
# Copy this file there, rename it (drop the .example), and edit.
#
# One source per line.  "Label | URL"  (label optional; a bare URL works too).
# Lines starting with # are ignored.  Each run overwrites <dir>/research/<slug>.md
# so the knowledge base always has the latest, never stale copies.

MMGA site            | https://mmga.agency
# Competitor blog     | https://somecompetitor.example/blog
# Industry news       | https://news.example/topic/marketing
# A client's pricing  | https://client.example/pricing
